# Resource Burner API — IntelliJ HTTP Client
# Select environment (dev/production) in the run gutter; base URLs live in http-client.env.json
#
# Tuning params on the start endpoints (all optional):
#   everySeconds — growth step interval, seconds (1-3600, default 10)
#   threads      — CPU burner threads added per step (1-256, default 1)
#   chunkMB      — RAM chunk retained per step, MB (1-1024, default 50)
# Re-calling start while growing retunes the speed without restarting.

### Status
GET {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/status

### CPU + RAM: start (default speed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/start

### CPU + RAM: start — really fast
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/start?everySeconds=1&threads=4&chunkMB=500

### CPU + RAM: start — really slow
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/start?everySeconds=600&threads=1&chunkMB=10

### CPU + RAM: stop (freeze growth, keep load)
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/stop

### CPU + RAM: clean (release everything)
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/clean

### CPU: start (default speed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/cpu/start

### CPU: start — really fast
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/cpu/start?everySeconds=1&threads=8

### CPU: start — really slow
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/cpu/start?everySeconds=600&threads=1

### CPU: stop
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/cpu/stop

### CPU: clean
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/cpu/clean

### RAM: start (default speed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/ram/start

### RAM: start — really fast
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/ram/start?everySeconds=1&chunkMB=500

### RAM: start — really slow
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/ram/start?everySeconds=600&chunkMB=10

### RAM: stop
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/ram/stop

### RAM: clean
POST {{baseUrl}}/resource-burner/ram/clean
